  },
  "question": {
    "text": "In a potentiometer experiment, the balancing length obtained with a cell is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>240</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. On shunting the cell with a resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>, the balancing length becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The internal resistance of the cell is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#xA0;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#x3A9;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#xA0;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#x3A9;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.5</mn><mo>&#xA0;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#x3A9;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the first case, the emf of the battery is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext>Kl</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;is the potential gradient and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is the first balancing length.</p><p>In the second case the potential difference across the battery is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mtext>ER</mtext><mrow><mtext>r</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>R</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext>Kl</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></math>,&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;is the shunt resistance used.</p><p>Dividing the above two equations, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mpadded lspace=\"+1px\"><mn>1</mn></mpadded><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#8658;r</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>240</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>120</mn></mrow><mn>120</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p>"
  }
}